runScript(file, coordinatorPort) -> exit status
    Resolve, read and parse the file; report failures before spawning.
    Start a separate one-shot coordinator with an isolated broker environment.
    Bound startup, evaluation and shutdown with an aggregate deadline.
    Forward output, wait for completion and clean up owned descendants.
    Return failure if starting or running the child failed; otherwise success.

runTests(optional files) -> exit status
    Discover executable test files when explicit names are absent.
    Reject an empty discovery result.
    Run each file in a separate runtime, continuing after failures.
    Print each result and the final counts; fail if any file failed.
